c stem cells\\nAnjali Cremer, Goethe University Hospital Frankfurt, Germany\\nTopic: Mechanisms of response and resistance to CD38 blocking in adult R/R T-ALL\\nTomas Jelinek, University of Ostrava, Czechia\\nTopic: Tumor microenvironment and clonal evolution in myeloma extramedullary disease\\nTopics-in-Focus Advanced Research Grant\\nMegane Brusson, Imagine Institute, \"}, {\"doc_id\": \"web-b6c9d3593c6121cf0281911b\", \"title\": \"2026 winners - The European Hematology Association (EHA)2026 winners - The European Hematology Association (EHA)\", \"source_ranges\": [{\"start\": 4069, \"end\": 4126, \"excerpt_start\": 0, \"excerpt_end\": 57}, {\"start\": 4231, \"end\": 5774, \"excerpt_start\": 58, \"excerpt_end\": 1601}], \"navigation_excerpt\": true, \"text\": \"Left Sidebar\\n8 min read · June 2, 2026\\nJune 2, 2026\\nShare\\n2026 winners\\nJunior Research Grant\\nMartina Sarchi, University of Pavia, Italy\\nTopic: ExIT-SF3B1: cell Extrinsic and Intrinsic mis-splicing-induced mechanisms and Therapeutic targets in SF3B1-mutant myelodysplastic neoplasms\\nPetr Danek, Institute of Organic Chemistry and Biochemistry of the CAS, Czechia\\nTopic: Chemically altered undigestible DNA: the driver of adverse effects associated with Busulfan/Cyclophosphamide treatment\\nNoémie Jollive, EFS INSERM U1255, France\\nTopic: Mechanobiology of the Blood-Bone Marrow Barrier after Pre-Transplant Conditioning and Its Role in HSPC Homing\\nPaula Rodriguez Marques, Amsterdam University Medical Center, The Netherlands\\nTopic: CAR-T Associated hematotoxicity: Resolving Mechanisms to reveal therapeutic Approaches\\nAdvanced Research Grant\\nAlyssa Cull, University of York, United Kingdom\\nTopic: Fanning the Flames: Characterising the Role of Macrophages in Blood Cancer Development\\nFranziska Auer, Technical University Munich, University Hospital, Germany\\nTopic: Determinants of Leukemia Predisposition and Therapy Resistance in PAX5-Driven B-ALL\\nMarlies Vanden Bempt, KU Leuven, Belgium\\nTopic: EZH2 mutations in clonal hematopoiesis and ETP-like ALL: a common mechanism?\\nPhysician Scientist Research Grant\\nNikolett Wohner, Semmelweis University, Hungary\\nTopic: Neutrophil Extracellular Traps: Basic Mechanisms and Clinical Implications\\nEtienne Crickx, Henri Mondor Hospital, France\\nTopic: Exploring humoral responses in delayed hemolytic transfusion reactions\\nFederica Barzaghi, IRCCS Ospedale San \"}, {\"doc_id\": \"web-81c57feef95692fb83b63747\", \"title\": \"EHA Bilateral Collaborative Grant - The European Hematology Association (EHA)EHA Bilateral Collaborative Grant - The European Hematology Association (EHA)\", \"source_ranges\": [{\"start\": 4082, \"end\": 4115, \"excerpt_start\": 0, \"excerpt_end\": 33}, {\"start\": 4184, \"end\": 4239, \"excerpt_start\": 34, \"excerpt_end\": 89}, {\"start\": 4578, \"end\": 6090, \"excerpt_start\": 90, \"excerpt_end\": 1602}], \"navigation_excerpt\": true, \"text\": \"EHA Bilateral Collaborative Grant\\nLeft Sidebar\\n3 min read · May 6, 2025\\nMay 6, 2025\\nShare\\nThe call has closed. Winners will be announced by mid-April 2027.\\nEHA Bilateral Collaborative Grants support collaboration between two independent research groups with complementarity of expertise and showing a mutual need to answer a specific research question.\\nSuccessful applicants can receive up to €320,000 for two years to be divided equally between the two research groups .\\nEligibility\\nYou’re eligible if:\\nBoth principal investigators (PIs) are EHA members\\nBoth PIs are basic and/or translational researchers\\nBoth PIs are independent researchers or group leaders and have full appointments at academic institutes or proven equivalents\\nThe PIs conduct their research in two different countries in Europe\\nAt least one of the PIs is a junior independent group leader, within five years of conducting independent research\\nNote: If an applicant is a physician scientist, at least 50% of their time should be dedicated to lab research\\nUnfortunately, you are not eligible if your proposal relates to:\\nPurely clinical research projects\\nProjects in health economics\\nOther non-lab-based research\\nTopics-in-Focus Bilateral Collaborative Grants: If your research focuses on hemoglobinopathies, you will have a competitive advantage in the selection process. Please select the ‘Topics-in-Focus Bilateral Collaborative Grant’ on your application form.\\nExtending the reach of our grants: If you are operating in a country less-represented among EHA grantees, you will have a competitive advantage in the selection proce\"}, {\"doc_id\": \"web-e00b0a496819dad9ea1b68ec\", \"title\": \"EHA Research Grants - The European Hematology Association (EHA)EHA Research Grants - The European Hematology Association (EHA)\", \"source_ranges\": [{\"start\": 4026, \"end\": 4045, \"excerpt_start\": 0, \"excerpt_end\": 19}, {\"start\": 4100, \"end\": 4159, \"excerpt_start\": 20, \"excerpt_end\": 79}, {\"start\": 4536, \"end\": 6058, \"excerpt_start\": 80, \"excerpt_end\": 1602}], \"navigation_excerpt\": true, \"text\": \"EHA Research Grants\\nLeft Sidebar\\n2 min read · June 16, 2026\\nJune 16, 2026\\nShare\\nThe call has closed. Winners will be announced by mid-April 2027.\\nEHA Research Grants are designed to support the future of hematology by helping talented junior researchers to:\\nConduct basic or translational lab-based research\\nGain valuable research and leadership experience\\nMove towards becoming group leaders\\nAdvance their careers\\nYou’re eligible if:\\nYou’re an EHA member\\nYour institute is an academic research center or proven equivalent in Europe\\nYou have the support of an academic department and institute\\nYour application relates to basic and translational lab-based research in hematology\\nYour application will not be eligible if it relates to:\\nPurely clinical research projects\\nProjects in health economics\\nOther non-lab-based research\\nHowever, it may be eligible if it relates to the translational part of a clinical trial. In this case, it must be both relevant and novel.\\nTypes of EHA Research Grants\\nThe three types of EHA Research Grant are the:\\nEHA Junior Research Grant, which can provide up to €150,000 for three years\\nEHA Advanced Research Grant, which can provide up to €240,000 for three years\\nEHA Physician Scientist Research Grant, which can provide up to €240,000 for three years\\nEach one of the three types of EHA Research Grant also has its own specific eligibility criteria. Please make sure you read the eligibility criteria for your grant type before you apply.\\nTopics-in-Focus Research Grants: If your research focuses on hemoglobinopathies, you will have a competitive advantage in the sele\"}, {\"doc_id\": \"web-327ebeb04d5b2145598d742a\", \"title\": \"EHA Grants Hall of Fame - The European Hematology Association (EHA)EHA Grants Hall of Fame - The European Hematology Association (EHA)\", \"source_ranges\": [{\"start\": 16553, \"end\": 16632, \"excerpt_start\": 0, \"excerpt_end\": 79}, {\"start\": 16873, \"end\": 16893, \"excerpt_start\": 80, \"excerpt_end\": 100}], \"navigation_excerpt\": true, \"text\": \"2026 winners\\n2025 winners\\n2024 winners\\n2023 winners\\nPrevious winners, 2012–2022\\nBecome an EHA Mentor\"}, {\"doc_id\": \"web-307533c1a4508473094316ab\", \"title\": \"Empowering progress, knowledge, and partnership. - The European Hematology Association (EHA)Empowering progress, knowledge, and partnership. - The European Hematology Association (EHA)\", \"source_ranges\": [{\"start\": 4142, \"end\": 5742, \"excerpt_start\": 0, \"excerpt_end\": 1600}], \"navigation_excerpt\": true, \"text\": \"Empowering progress, knowledge, and partnership.\\nWelcome to Borderless Hematology.\\nEHA is the leading force in hematology, bringing the community together to share knowledge, collaborate, connect, and grow.\\nTogether we accelerate progress through education, science, and innovation. Together we improve patient outcomes an