nter, The Netherlands\\nTopic: CAR-T Associated hematotoxicity: Resolving Mechanisms to reveal therapeutic Approaches\\nAdvanced Research Grant\\nAlyssa Cull, University of York, United Kingdom\\nTopic: Fanning the Flames: Characterising the Role of Macrophages in Blood Cancer Development\\nFranziska Auer, Technical University Munich, University Hospital, Germany\\nTopic: Determinants of Leukemia Predisposition and Therapy Resistance in PAX5-Driven B-ALL\\nMarlies Vanden Bempt, KU Leuven, Belgium\\nTopic: EZH2 mutations in clonal hematopoiesis and ETP-like ALL: a common mechanism?\\nPhysician Scientist Research Grant\\nNikolett Wohner, Semmelweis University, Hungary\\nTopic: Neutrophil Extracellular Traps: Basic Mechanisms and Clinical Implications\\nEtienne Crickx, Henri Mondor Hospital, France\\nTopic: Exploring humoral responses in delayed hemolytic transfusion reactions\\nFederica Barzaghi, IRCCS Ospedale San \"}, {\"doc_id\": \"web-307533c1a4508473094316ab\", \"title\": \"Empowering progress, knowledge, and partnership. - The European Hematology Association (EHA)Empowering progress, knowledge, and partnership. - The European Hematology Association (EHA)\", \"source_ranges\": [{\"start\": 4142, \"end\": 5742, \"excerpt_start\": 0, \"excerpt_end\": 1600}], \"navigation_excerpt\": true, \"text\": \"Empowering progress, knowledge, and partnership.\\nWelcome to Borderless Hematology.\\nEHA is the leading force in hematology, bringing the community together to share knowledge, collaborate, connect, and grow.\\nTogether we accelerate progress through education, science, and innovation. Together we improve patient outcomes and progress towards cures—across Europe and beyond.\\nTogether, the future of hematology is within our reach.\\nJoin us with membership that works for you or learn more about our story.\\nEHA2027 Congress\\nEuropean affairs\\nEHA Campus\\nGrants\\nSpecialized Working Groups\\nWhat’s new?\\nGo to overview\\nTuesday, September 29, 2026\\nEHA's Long-Term Advocacy for Hematology Achieves a Major Milestone\\nTuesday, September 22, 2026\\nInterview with EHA’s European Affairs Committee Member, Ariane Weinman\\nThursday, July 23, 2026\\nASCERTAIN project for better pricing and reimbursement models enters final phase\\nWednesday, July 22, 2026\\nInterview with EHA’s European Affairs Committee Member, Kate Morgan\\nMonday, July 6, 2026\\nPublication of EHA Annual General Meeting 2026 minutes\\nReady to join our community?\\nOur network is not just a professional association; it’s a community that nurtures growth, membership, and innovation in a manner that transcends geographical and intellectual borders. To us, this is Borderless Hematology.\\nJoin EHA today\\nEHA Mentorship Program\\nBecome a mentor today\\nMentoring is about more than sharing knowledge. It’s about building connections, gaining fresh perspectives, and helping shape the future of hematology.\\nIf you believe in the power of community and want to suppo\"}, {\"doc_id\": \"web-81c57feef95692fb83b63747\", \"title\": \"EHA Bilateral Collaborative Grant - The European Hematology Association (EHA)EHA Bilateral Collaborative Grant - The European Hematology Association (EHA)\", \"source_ranges\": [{\"start\": 4082, \"end\": 4115, \"excerpt_start\": 0, \"excerpt_end\": 33}, {\"start\": 4184, \"end\": 4239, \"excerpt_start\": 34, \"excerpt_end\": 89}, {\"start\": 4578, \"end\": 6090, \"excerpt_start\": 90, \"excerpt_end\": 1602}], \"navigation_excerpt\": true, \"text\": \"EHA Bilateral Collaborative Grant\\nLeft Sidebar\\n3 min read · May 6, 2025\\nMay 6, 2025\\nShare\\nThe call has closed. Winners will be announced by mid-April 2027.\\nEHA Bilateral Collaborative Grants support collaboration between two independent research groups with complementarity of expertise and showing a mutual need to answer a specific research question.\\nSuccessful applicants can receive up to €320,000 for two years to be divided equally between the two research groups .\\nEligibility\\nYou’re eligible if:\\nBoth principal investigators (PIs) are EHA members\\nBoth PIs are basic and/or translational researchers\\nBoth PIs are independent researchers or group leaders and have full appointments at academic institutes or proven equivalents\\nThe PIs conduct their research in two different countries in Europe\\nAt least one of the PIs is a junior independent group leader, within five years of conducting independent research\\nNote: If an applicant is a physician scientist, at least 50% of their time should be dedicated to lab research\\nUnfortunately, you are not eligible if your proposal relates to:\\nPurely clinical research projects\\nProjects in health economics\\nOther non-lab-based research\\nTopics-in-Focus Bilateral Collaborative Grants: If your research focuses on hemoglobinopathies, you will have a competitive advantage in the selection process. Please select the ‘Topics-in-Focus Bilateral Collaborative Grant’ on your application form.\\nExtending the reach of our grants: If you are operating in a country less-represented among EHA grantees, you will have a competitive advantage in the selection proce\"}, {\"doc_id\": \"web-327ebeb04d5b2145598d742a\", \"title\": \"EHA Grants Hall of Fame - The European Hematology Association (EHA)EHA Grants Hall of Fame - The European Hematology Association (EHA)\", \"source_ranges\": [{\"start\": 16553, \"end\": 16632, \"excerpt_start\": 0, \"excerpt_end\": 79}, {\"start\": 16873, \"end\": 16893, \"excerpt_start\": 80, \"excerpt_end\": 100}], \"navigation_excerpt\": true, \"text\": \"2026 winners\\n2025 winners\\n2024 winners\\n2023 winners\\nPrevious winners, 2012–2022\\nBecome an EHA Mentor\"}], \"local_exploration\": {\"visited_doc_ids\": [\"web-307533c1a4508473094316ab\", \"web-f3aba4b966c28f155f997043\", \"web-e00b0a496819dad9ea1b68ec\", \"web-327ebeb04d5b2145598d742a\", \"web-81c57feef95692fb83b63747\", \"web-b6c9d3593c6121cf0281911b\", \"web-2635c387c9601a1d760ec385\", \"web-ece509e1ea7055ce41222f0