"main\", \"source_context\": {\"start\": 4126, \"end\": 4306, \"text\": \"ies\\nLeft Sidebar\\n1 min read · May 6, 2025\\nMay 6, 2025\\nShare\\nGrants\\nEHA Research Grants\\nEHA Bilateral Collaborative Grant\\nEHA Innovation Grant\\nEHA Kick-off Grant\\nEHA Research Mobili\"}}, {\"id\": \"l114\", \"source_doc_id\": \"web-ece509e1ea7055ce41222f0b\", \"url\": \"https://ehaweb.org/research-innovation/grants/non-eha-funding-opportunities/dkms-john-hansen-research-grant\", \"text\": \"DKMS John Hansen Research Grant\", \"source_region\": \"main\", \"source_context\": {\"start\": 4593, \"end\": 4773, \"text\": \"e, please contact [email protected].\\nCurrent opportunities:\\nDKMS John Hansen Research Grant\\nShare\\nGrants\\nEHA Research Grants\\nEHA Bilateral Collaborative Grant\\nEHA Innovation Grant\\n\"}}, {\"id\": \"l155\", \"source_doc_id\": \"web-e00b0a496819dad9ea1b68ec\", \"url\": \"https://ehaweb.org/research-innovation/grants/about-our-eha-research-grants/eha-research-grant-review-and-selection-process/\", \"text\": \"EHA Research Grant review and selection process\", \"source_region\": \"main\", \"source_context\": {\"start\": 6586, \"end\": 6766, \"text\": \"for an EHA Research Grant\\nWhat an EHA Research Grant covers\\nEHA Research Grant review and selection process\\nShare\\nGrants\\nEHA Research Grants\\nHow to apply for an EHA Research Grant\\n\"}}, {\"id\": \"l156\", \"source_doc_id\": \"web-f3aba4b966c28f155f997043\", \"url\": \"https://ehaweb.org/research-innovation/grants/non-eha-funding-opportunities/\", \"text\": \"funding from non-EHA sources\", \"source_region\": \"main\", \"source_context\": {\"start\": 4681, \"end\": 4861, \"text\": \"n this section, you can also learn about EHA Travel Grants, funding from non-EHA sources and browse our grant-winners hall of fame.\\nEHA Advanced Research Grant\\nEHA Bilateral Collab\"}}, {\"id\": \"l157\", \"source_doc_id\": \"web-f3aba4b966c28f155f997043\", \"url\": \"https://ehaweb.org/research-innovation/grants/eha-advanced-research-grant\", \"text\": \"EHA Advanced Research Grant\", \"source_region\": \"main\", \"source_context\": {\"start\": 4753, \"end\": 4933, \"text\": \" non-EHA sources and browse our grant-winners hall of fame.\\nEHA Advanced Research Grant\\nEHA Bilateral Collaborative Grant\\nEHA Innovation Grant\\nEHA Junior Research Grant\\nEHA Kick-of\"}}, {\"id\": \"l158\", \"source_doc_id\": \"web-f3aba4b966c28f155f997043\", \"url\": \"https://ehaweb.org/research-innovation/grants/eha-junior-research-grant\", \"text\": \"EHA Junior Research Grant\", \"source_region\": \"main\", \"source_context\": {\"start\": 4836, \"end\": 5016, \"text\": \"rant\\nEHA Bilateral Collaborative Grant\\nEHA Innovation Grant\\nEHA Junior Research Grant\\nEHA Kick-off Grant\\nEHA Physician Scientist Research Grant\\nEHA Research Mobility Grant\\nJoin EHA\"}}, {\"id\": \"l159\", \"source_doc_id\": \"web-f3aba4b966c28f155f997043\", \"url\": \"https://ehaweb.org/research-innovation/grants/eha-physician-scientist-research-grant\", \"text\": \"EHA Physician Scientist Research Grant\", \"source_region\": \"main\", \"source_context\": {\"start\": 4881, \"end\": 5061, \"text\": \"novation Grant\\nEHA Junior Research Grant\\nEHA Kick-off Grant\\nEHA Physician Scientist Research Grant\\nEHA Research Mobility Grant\\nJoin EHA\\nFull membership\\nJunior membership\\n60-day tri\"}}], \"supported_parent_doc_ids\": [], \"source_pages\": [{\"doc_id\": \"web-c03ac93bf969f633bdee1f34\", \"title\": \"How to apply for an EHA Innovation Grant - The European Hematology Association (EHA)How to apply for an EHA Innovation Grant - The European Hematology Association (EHA)\", \"source_ranges\": [{\"start\": 4206, \"end\": 4261, \"excerpt_start\": 0, \"excerpt_end\": 55}, {\"start\": 4374, \"end\": 5919, \"excerpt_start\": 56, \"excerpt_end\": 1601}], \"navigation_excerpt\": true, \"text\": \"Left Sidebar\\n5 min read · May 6, 2025\\nMay 6, 2025\\nShare\\nHow to apply for an EHA Innovation Grant\\nHere you will find an overview of the actions you’ll need to take when submitting an EHA Innovation Grant application. You can also refer to our Innovation Grants Application Checklist.\\nBefore you begin\\nMake sure you’ve read and understood:\\nThe information on eligibility and how you can use the funding on the main EHA Innovation Grant page\\nOur policy on life events\\nOur policy on double awarding\\nYou’ll also need to share our EHA Innovation Grant Agreement Template with your heads of department and institutional representatives. It’s important that these individuals include a statement, in their support letters, that they understand and agree to the conditions in the grant agreement from the outset.\\nPlease note that at this stage you do not need to fill in the grant agreement template or get it signed.\\nEHA Portal account\\nTo apply, you must be registered on the EHA Portal.\\nOnly one principal investigator (PI 1) must submit the application on behalf of the collaboration. However, all PIs must create separate profiles on the EHA Portal and provide personal details.\\nIf you already have an EHA Portal account\\nYou can either:\\nLog in using your existing credentials\\nSelect ‘Reset or create password’ if you cannot remember your details\\nWhen you log in, make sure you use the email address that EHA has on file.\\nIf you do not have an EHA Portal account\\nGo to the EHA Portal and follow the steps under the ‘Create your user profile’ heading.\\nPlease keep in mind that, once you register, it may take\"}, {\"doc_id\": \"web-8696582e313512830ddfba30\", \"title\": \"EHA Innovation Grant - The European Hematology Association (EHA)EHA Innovation Grant - The European Hematology Association (EHA)\", \"source_ranges\": [{\"start\": 4030, \"end\": 4050, \"excerpt_start\": 0, \"excerpt_end\": 20}, {\"start\": 4106, \"end\": 4161, \"excerpt_start\": 21, \"excerpt_end\": 76}, {\"start\": 4474, \"end\": 5999, \"excerpt_start\": 77, \"excerpt_end\": 1602}], \"navigation_excerpt\": true, \"text\": \"EHA Innovation Grant\\nLeft Sidebar\\n4 min read · May 6, 2025\\nMay 6, 2025\\nShare\\nPlease be advised that the call for applications for the 2027 cycle will not open this year. If you would like to be notified when the next application cycle opens, please join our mailing list by contacting us at [email protected].\\nEHA Innovation Grants encourage and support the:\\nCreation of consortia\\nGeneration of preliminary data that can then be used to apply for larger funding opportunities\\nThe grants:\\nSupport high-quality clinical or translational research in hematology\\nLast for a period of two years\\nCan provide a total award of up to €300,000 for the whole consortium\\nEligibility\\nEvery principal investigator (PI) must be an EHA member.\\nAll PIs must be conducting high-quality clinical or translational research. Basic and/or translational researchers can also be included, but the general focus of the project must remain clinical and translational.\\nAll PIs must be independent researchers or group leaders and have full appointments at academic institutes or proven equivalents in Europe.\\nEach consortium must include at least three PIs operating in at least three different countries in Europe.\\nAt least one of the PIs must operate in of the following countries: Albania, Armenia, Azerbaijan, Bosnia and Herzegovina, Bulgaria, Croatia, Estonia, Georgia, Hungary, Kosovo, Latvia, Lithuania, Moldova, Montenegro, North Macedonia, Poland, Portugal, Romania, Serbia, Slovak Republic, Slovenia, Türkiye, Ukraine.\\nAt least one of the PIs must be a junior independent group leader, within five years of conducting in\"}, {\"doc_id\": \"web-c60022ff9847a5c52747af0c\", \"title\": \"Precision Hematology Topics-in-Focus program - The European Hematology Association (EHA)Precision Hematology Topics-in-Focus program - The European Hematology Association (EHA)\", \"source_ranges\": [{\"start\": 4126, \"end\": 4170, \"excerpt_start\": 0, \"excerpt_end\": 44}, {\"start\": 4267, \"end\": 4324, \"excerpt_start\": 45, \"excerpt_end\": 102}, {\"start\": 4437, \"end\": 5936, \"excerpt_start\": 103, \"excerpt_end\": 1602}], \"navigation_excerpt\": true, \"text\": \"Precision Hematology Topics-in-Focus program\\nLeft Sidebar\\n2 min read · May 16, 2025\\nMay 16, 2025\\nShare\\nWhat is precision hematology?\\nPrecision hematology is an integrated approach to diagnosing and treating blood disorders—particularly hematologic malignancies—by leveraging detailed molecular, genetic, and functional information about each patient’s disease.\\nIt matches therapies more precisely to individual patients by uniting innovative clinical trial designs with cutting-edge diagnostics, such as:\\nAdvanced imaging\\nGenetic profiling\\nDrug-sensitivity testing\\nThis field brings together physicians, scientists, and other key stakeholders across preclinical, translational, and clinical research. Through this collaboration, precision hematology aims to:\\nAccelerate the discovery of new treatment strategies\\nRefine therapeutic decision-making\\nImprove outcomes for patients with blood cancers\\nOur program’s goals\\nOur Precision Hematology Topics-in-Focus program is designed to promote innovative concepts for diagnostics and innovative clinical trial designs which will feed into the clinical application of precision hematology.\\nThe goal of the program is to create a European regulatory framework for precision hematology. By increasing awareness and providing education, guidelines, and policies, we can improve access to:\\nDiagnostics\\nClinical research\\nTreatment in malignant hematology\\nUseful materials\\nEHA Position Paper on Personalized Treatment for Hematologic Diseases\\nPrecision Medicine in Hematology in 2021: Definitions, Tools, Perspectives, and Open Questions\\nIn Vitro Diagnostic Medical\"}, {\"doc_id\": \"web-ece509e1ea7055ce41222f0b\", \"title\": \"Non-EHA funding opportunities - The European Hematology Association (EHA)Non-EHA funding opportunities - The European Hematology Association (EHA)\", \"source_ranges\": [{\"start\": 4130, \"end\": 4185, \"excerpt_start\": 0, \"excerpt_end\": 55}, {\"start\": 4407, \"end\": 4690, \"excerpt_start\": 56, \"excerpt_end\": 339}, {\"start\": 5152, \"end\": 5172, \"excerpt_start\": 340, \"excerpt_end\": 360}], \"navigation_excerpt\": true, \"text\": \"Left Sidebar\\n1 min read · May 6, 2025\\nMay 6, 2025\\nShare\\nNon-EHA funding opportunities\\nOn this page, we’ll list other interesting funding opportunities for European researchers in hematology.\\nIf you’d like us to add any opportunity to this page, please contact [email protected].\\nCurrent opportunities:\\nDKMS John Hansen Research Grant\\nShare\\nBecome an EHA Mentor\"}, {\"doc_id\": \"web-e00b0a496819dad9ea1b68ec\", \"title\": \"EHA Research Grants - The European Hematology Association (EHA)EHA Research Grants - The European Hematology Association (EHA)\", \"source_ranges\": [{\"start\": 4026, \"end\": 4045, \"excerpt_start\": 0, \"excerpt_end\": 19}, {\"start\": 4100, \"end\": 4159, \"excerpt_start\": 20, \"excerpt_end\": 79}, {\"start\": 4536, \"end\": 6058, \"excerpt_start\": 80, \"excerpt_end\": 1602}], \"navigation_excerpt\": true, \"text\": \"EHA Research Grants\\nLeft Sidebar\\n2 min read · June 16, 2026\\nJune 16, 2026\\nShare\\nThe call has closed. Winners will be announced by mid-April 2027.\\nEHA Research Grants are designed to support the future of hematology by helping talented junior researchers to:\\nConduct basic or translational lab-based research\\nGain valuable research and leadership experience\\nMove towards becoming group leaders\\nAdvance their careers\\nYou’re eligible if:\\nYou’re an EHA member\\nYour institute is an academic research center or proven equivalent in Europe\\nYou have the support of an academic department and institute\\nYour application relates to basic and translational lab-based research in hematology\\nYour application will not be eligible if it relates to:\\nPurely clinical research projects\\nProjects in health economics\\nOther non-lab-based research\\nHowever, it may be eligible if it relates to the translational part of a clinical trial. In this case, it must be both relevant and novel.\\nTypes of EHA Research Grants\\nThe three types of EHA Research Grant are the:\\nEHA Junior Research Grant, which can provide up to €150,000 for three years\\nEHA Advanced Research Grant, which can provide up to €240,000 for three years\\nEHA Physician Scientist Research Grant, which can provide up to €240,000 for three years\\nEach one of the three types of EHA Research Grant also has its own specific eligibility criteria. Please make sure you read the eligibility criteria for your grant type before you apply.\\nTopics-in-Focus Research Grants: If your research focuses on hemoglobinopathies, you will have a competitive advantage in the sele\"}, {\"doc_id\": \"web-f3aba4b966c28f155f997043\", \"title\": \"Grants - The European Hematology Association (EHA)Grants - The European Hematology Association (EHA)\", \"source_ranges\": [{\"start\": 3974, \"end\": 5007, \"excerpt_start\": 0, \"excerpt_end\": 1033}, {\"start\": 5248, \"end\": 5268, \"excerpt_start\": 1034, \"excerpt_end\": 1054}], \"navigation_excerpt\": true, \"text\": \"Grants\\nEHA’s foundations are built upon our belief that it’s the collective endeavors of our community—in research and clinical practice—that lead to exponential advancements.\\nWe’re committed to accelerating progress in hematology by promoting collaboration, education, and research across all levels.\\nAn important way of achieving this is through the careful and selective allocation of grants and funding to aspiring scientists and researchers.\\nTo check which of our grants you can apply for, use the filters below. Alternatively, you can read about our different grant categories:\\nEHA Research Grants\\nEHA Bilateral Collaborative Grant\\nEHA Innovation Grant\\nEHA Kick-off Grant\\nEH