ission statement\",\"time_scope\":\"agreement\"}},\"documents\":[{\"doc_id\":\"web-8760a0a79ab2a9cd59bad81b\",\"earliest_visible_original\":{\"id\":\"s7\",\"doc_id\":\"web-8760a0a79ab2a9cd59bad81b\",\"start\":0,\"end\":356,\"text\":\"ICSE News\\nICSE News\\nICSE\\nInternational Conference\\non Software Engineering®\\nHOME\\nNews from the SC\\nEDI STATEMENT\\nCONDUCT & SAFETY\\nHISTORY\\nPROCEEDINGS\\nINFLUENTIAL PAPERS\\nORGANIZING ICSE\\nSTEERING COMMITTEE\\nICSE SC Documents\\nSPONSORS\\nCONTACTS\\nLast updated\\nJan 2026\\nNews from the SC\\nDec 20, 2025:\\nTokyo Selected to Host ICSE 2029\\nBy ICSE Tokyo Bidding Committee\\n\",\"source_role\":\"document\",\"source_message_indices\":[],\"time_metadata\":{}}}]},\"cards\":[]},\"original_question\":\"When and where was the ICSE duplicate submission statement agreed upon?\",\"task\":{\"question\":\"When and where was the ICSE duplicate submission statement agreed upon?\",\"output_slot\":\"agreement_details\",\"answer_type\":\"record\",\"inputs\":[],\"execution\":\"retrieval\"},\"grounded_subquestion\":\"When and where was the ICSE duplicate submission statement agreed upon?\",\"request_context\":{\"query_identity\":\"191045398490653521e8bac0cdc04efa9fb82781a902f44495093422136b6d68\",\"algorithm_version\":\"dagbt_residual_memory_v2\",\"program_identity\":\"1611e508381f00f01fbede86fa2fc6ffb12a01667f2eddbc48c7cb2eda8e96bd\",\"initial_dag_identity\":\"7a8c206e30afbad778ff12a979d967523991179bb94edf5c8479e76fc78b3857\"},\"variables\":{\"time\":{\"type\":\"text\",\"demand\":\"agreement_details\",\"open\":true,\"scope\":{\"entity_scope\":\"ICSE duplicate submission statement\",\"time_scope\":\"agreement\"}},\"place\":{\"type\":\"entity\",\"demand\":\"agreement_details\",\"open\":true,\"scope\":{\"entity_scope\":\"ICSE duplicate submission statement\",\"time_scope\":\"agreement\"}}},\"requested_slots\":[\"time\",\"place\"],\"requested_scopes\":{\"time\":{\"entity_scope\":\"ICSE duplicate submission statement\",\"time_scope\":\"agreement\"},\"place\":{\"entity_scope\":\"ICSE duplicate submission statement\",\"time_scope\":\"agreement\"}},\"output_contract\":{\"mode\":\"value\",\"result_type\":\"record\",\"entity_scope\":\"ICSE duplicate submission statement\",\"time_scope\":\"agreement\",\"explanation\":\"none\",\"fields\":[\"time\",\"place\"]},\"program_revision\":0,\"rule_binding\":null,\"supported_parents\":{},\"known_observations\":[],\"source_spans\":[[\"s7\",\"d1\",0,356,\"ICSE News\\nICSE News\\nICSE\\nInternational Conference\\non Software Engineering®\\nHOME\\nNews from the SC\\nEDI STATEMENT\\nCONDUCT & SAFETY\\nHISTORY\\nPROCEEDINGS\\nINFLUENTIAL PAPERS\\nORGANIZING ICSE\\nSTEERING COMMITTEE\\nICSE SC Documents\\nSPONSORS\\nCONTACTS\\nLast updated\\nJan 2026\\nNews from the SC\\nDec 20, 2025:\\nTokyo Selected to Host ICSE 2029\\nBy ICSE Tokyo Bidding Committee\\n\",\"document\",[]],[\"s8\",\"d1\",356,747,\"The ICSE Tokyo Bidding Committee is thrilled and deeply honored that the ICSE Steering\\nCommittee has selected Tokyo as the host city for the 51st International Conference on\\nSoftware Engineering (ICSE 2029).\\nJapan has proudly hosted ICSE twice before - ICSE 1982 in Tokyo and ICSE 1998 in Kyoto. After\\nnearly 30 years, ICSE is finally returning to Japan, and we are delighted to welcome the\\n\",\"document\",[]],[\"s9\",\"d1\",747,1103,\"community back to Tokyo, starting the next 50 years of ICSE. As Japan’s capital, Tokyo is\\nconsistently recognized as one of the safest cities in the world and is among the most\\ndynamic and populous metropolitan areas globally, regularly topping travelers’ rankings.\\nThe Japanese software engineering community, represented by IPSJ-SIGSE together with many\\n\",\"document\",[]],[\"s10\",\"d1\",1103,1441,\"other groups - including IEICE SIG-SS, SIG-KBSE, JSSST FOSE, MLSE, and rePiT - has been\\nsteadily growing and strengthening its research and practice activities. These efforts have\\ncreated vibrant, long-standing nationwide networks of researchers, practitioners, and\\neducators, supported by strong and active international collaborations.\\n\",\"document\",[]],[\"s11\",\"d1\",1441,1805,\"The Japanese software engineering community is proud to welcome ICSE 2029 to Tokyo, with the\\ngenerous support of the Tokyo Convention & Visitors Bureau and valued sponsors. Hosting ICSE\\n2029 marks a historic milestone for Japan and the broader region, strengthening global\\ncollaboration and partnerships across academia, industry, and government. Bringing ICSE to\\n\",\"document\",[]],[\"s12\",\"d1\",1805,2196,\"Tokyo will also broaden participation from around the world and provide exciting\\nopportunities to connect with leading industries in AI, quantum computing, electrical\\nengineering, manufacturing, robotics, automotive systems, and beyond, all of which are\\nstrong in Japan and the broader Asian region.\\nWe are fully committed to dedicating all necessary resources to deliver an outstanding and\\n\",\"document\",[]],[\"s13\",\"d1\",2196,2544,\"memorable ICSE. We cannot wait to welcome you to Tokyo in 2029!\\nICSE 2029 General Chairs: Hironori Washizaki and Jianjun Zhao\\nDec 5, 2025: ICSE\\nCall for Letters of Interest to Host ICSE 2030\\nBy\\nArie van Deursen and Margaret-Anne Storey\\nThe ICSE Steering Committee now invites the\\nsubmission of Letters of Interest (LoI) to host ICSE in April 2030.\\n\",\"document\",[]],[\"s14\",\"d1\",2544,2865,\"ICSE is the premier international forum for researchers and practitioners to present and\\ndiscuss\\nthe most recent innovations, trends, outcomes, experiences, and challenges in the field of\\nsoftware engineering.\\nThe conference is hosted around the world, and 2030 is the year for ICSE to be hosted in a\\nlocation in Europe.\\n\",\"document\",[]],[\"s15\",\"d1\",2865,3261,\"The letters of Interests are meant to inform the Steering Committee of potential available\\nteams and sites and they are not binding.\\nPlease do not make any commitments to prospective venues or organizing members as the\\nsubmission\\nof the letter is just one piece in a more extensive\\nevaluation process.\\nDetails of submission:\\nLetter: A one-page document must include (more details can be found at\\n\",\"document\",[]],[\"s16\",\"d1\",3261,3660,\"this\\ndocumentation)\\nSubmitter contact information .\\nOrganizing core team .\\nCity and potential venues\\nBrief description of local software engineering community (academic and\\nindustrial)\\nthat would support and participate in the conference\\nAttributes of the site that would make it appealing for attendees\\nExpected impact to the local and global software engineering community\\nDeadline: March 1, 2026\\n\",\"document\",[]],[\"s17\",\"d1\",3660,4007,\"Procedure: Email letter in pdf to the ICSE SC co-chairs:\\narie.vandeursen@tudelft.nl\\nand mstorey@uvic.ca.\\nSep 15, 2025: ICSE\\nResearch Track will Move to Single Cycle\\nBy\\nArie van Deursen and Margaret-Anne Storey\\nFor\\nthe ICSE Research Track, the ICSE Steering Committee has decided to replace the two-cycle\\nsubmission process by a single cycle.\\nThis\\n\",\"document\",[]],[\"s18\",\"d1\",4007,4386,\"means that from ICSE 2027 onwards, the spring submission deadline for research papers will\\nbe dropped, leaving only the summer deadline. In particular, there will be no submission\\npossibility for ICSE research papers in the spring of 2026.\\nIn\\n2024, 2025, and 2026, the ICSE Research Track had two cycles. Cycle 1 commonly had a\\ndeadline in March, and cycle 2 a deadline in July. \",\"document\",[]],[\"s19\",\"d1\",4386,4768,\"The submission months of these cycles\\nwere aligned with the ASE and FSE conferences (with ICSE dubbed “SE3”), to provide\\ndeadlines spread over the year for major software engineering conferences.\\nAfter\\nthree years of two cycles a process was initiated to evaluate the two cycle system. This\\nincluded a (Mentimeter-based) session with the community during the Town Hall at ICSE 2025\\n\",\"document\",[]],[\"s20\",\"d1\",4768,5115,\"in Ottawa, as well as multiple discussions in the ICSE Steering Committee (before\\nand after the Town Hall). From this, the following key issues emerged:\\nAmong the three main\\nsoftware engineering conferences, ICSE is the only one with two cycles.\\nThe duration from\\ncycle 1 submission (March) to conference presentation (April the year after) is 13\\n\",\"document\",[]],[\"s21\",\"d1\",5115,5496,\"months, which is long in a rapidly evolving field (for presenters and audience at the\\nconference).\\nCycle 1 will take\\naway submissions and reviewer availability from other SE venues with deadlines in the\\nsame period (such as ASE)\\nDespite the long duration,\\nthere is substantial interest from authors to submit (654 submissions for Cycle 1 for\\nICSE 2026, up from 504 for ICSE 2025).\\n\",\"document\",[]],[\"s22\",\"d1\",5496,5868,\"The full submission\\nprocess with two cycles may appear complex to authors\\nFor reviewers, the\\nlong duration of the reviewing process, especially when involved in both cycles, is\\ndemanding.\\nThe\\ndiscussion of these issues did not lead to a clear consensus on whether to maintain the two\\ncycles. The overall sentiment was well described by one of the participants in the Town\\n\",\"document\",[]],[\"s23\",\"d1\",5868,6210,\"Hall: “I like it as an author but not as a reviewer. So very split”.\\nTo\\nreach a decision, an online vote was organized among the steering committee. With a small\\nmajority, the outcome of the vote was to move to a single cycle from ICSE 2027 onwards.\\nWe\\nthank everyone who contributed to the discussions. Besides the two cycles, many ideas on\\n\",\"document\",[]],[\"s24\",\"d1\",6210,6606,\"making ICSE and its paper reviewing process better have been brought up. These will be\\nfurther elaborated within the steering committee for use in future ICSE (or SE3)\\nconferences.\\nSep 1, 2025: Steering\\nCommittee Welcomes Six new Members\\nBy\\nArie van Deursen and Margaret-Anne Storey\\nIt\\nis with great pleasure that we welcome six new members to the ICSE Steering Committee.\\nICSE 2027 SEIP chairs:\\n\",\"document\",[]],[\"s25\",\"d1\",6606,6966,\"Helena Holmström-Olsson, Malmö University, homepage\\nAntonio Filieri, Amazon Web Services (AWS) and Imperial College London, homepage\\nICSE 2028 PC chairs:\\nYuanfang Cai, Drexel University, homepage\\nLars Grunske, Humboldt-Universität zu Berlin, homepage\\nICSE 2028 SEIP chairs:\\nQinghua Lu, CSIRO, homepage\\nJan Bosch, Chalmers University of Technology, homepage\\nWe\\n\",\"document\",[]],[\"s26\",\"d1\",6966,7274,\"are grateful that they will lead the Research Track of 2028, and the Software Engineering in\\nPractice tracks of 2027 and 2028. They will serve on the Steering Committee until 2030 and\\n2031, respectively, and thus will help shape the future of the ICSE conference\\nseries. We look forward to working with them!\",\"document\",[]]],\"required_scope\":{\"entity_scope\":\"ICSE duplicate submission statement\",\"time_scope\":\"agreement\"},\"rules_completion_required\":false,\"supported_task_outputs\":{},\"source_documents\":{\"d1\":{\"doc_id\":\"web-8760a0a79ab2a9cd59bad81b\",\"time_metadata\":{}}},\"source_span_columns\":[\"id\",\"doc_id\",\"start\",\"end\",\"text\",\"source_role\",\"source_message_indices\"]}"}], "logical_call_index": 5, "response_format": "plain", "input_tokens_local": 6561, "output_token_reserve": 4096, "input_margin": 256, "max_model_len": 120000, "tokenization_request_sha256": "a1f1ebeb108c298d866225ebad4a6ee8ebfb7b1885ee2d6de32ccd6fe72b1c83", "tokenization_endpoint_sha256": "0ed12ee94b55bfdbc62fb247243af2d71aa1d7ea503f5f191605ae295c5ad94a", "token_count_is_estimate": false, "token_estimator_id": "deployment_vllm_chat_v1", "tokenizer_id": null, "add_generation_prompt": true, "tokenization_scope": "adapted_plain_text_chat_default_server_template", "token_accounting_note": "Deployment input count; model weights and tokenizer hash